**Definition 8.2 (exact full expansion recurrence).** For every routine
here define its bill by fully expanding Definition 2.1 and ARC §10/RCA
Definition 11.5, with its actual entered heads, banks, tokens, retained
words and typed inputs. A native leaf has Definition 8.1's increments
and its actual successor. Sequence adds the next bill at the previous
complete successor. A test pays its actual RD/CTL and chosen branch;
a while pays every test, body and back edge in written order. Its
termination value has zero further rows only after the prescribed final
row. The recurrence's leaves, including every new operation, are fixed
by the following table; none is an unspecified unit-cost oracle.

| Contributor | Native leaves required in addition to the actual successor dependence |
| --- | --- |
| Initial apparatus | Original boot/preparation/validation/acquisition/client parking; twenty annex boundary constructors; all old/new owner/token/control bits; both bootstrap NEXT/IN/WRITE/ADVANCE/DONE sequences; full captured frame and descriptor/seal. |
| Initial registers/manifest | Actual $r_{\rm sel}$ unrolled empty fields, bank sentinels and descriptor; all original/capture/current descriptions and public fields; saved-head imports, symbol-triple cons, restore moves; every measured export and complete ManifestPrefix scan. |
| Every word assignment | Base, dry field-length emissions, LastBank/Field/LastScratch scans, real old/new field copies, separators/F/seal, descriptor count/write, parity/purpose CTLs and retained previous bank. |
| Mode and frame | Saved Base, all IN/EX/WR/MR and length tests, mode CTL, payload bound copy and tested append, F/seal, literal/measured lengths, descriptor scans/fields, native F-bounded imports, Reverse and persistent copies. |
| Parse/arithmetic | ReadList/ReadFrame/ReadUnary, each Take/cons/tail/test, payload exhaustion, copied unary cancellation/comparison/Cat, numeric wire zeros and every finite failure branch. |
| Source resolution | Whole frozen M traversal and unary item index, fixed CAP tuple parsing, origin/status/dependency/predecessor checks and full selected-item copies. |
| Anchor location | Represented entrance/reservoir construction; copy of $b$; each fixed-set/equality test on actual physical control; each Step row-table/cell/mark scan and replacement, token/latch/control update, receipt/event/tally serialization; all entry/exit tests/saves and countdown tails. |
| Cover and Issue | Actual cover/package cardinality, complete immutable list/backing copies, Boundary/Prefix, exact consumed $I_k$, whole tagged selector/binding fields, sender export/descriptor/seal. |
| Call | Its own immutable resolution and Prefix, full 74-port raw state/history serializer including raw control and permission data, copied Image and its new retained backing. |
| Each publication | Actual bases, allocations and initialized intervals; full descriptors; dry/real descriptor staging and its own descriptor; both endpoint seeks; fresh payload length copies; both tested copies; seals/TOKs and completion records; mandatory print. |
| Every callback/return | Placement recovery/Seek before bank work, clear/import/Reverse/tuple checks, full binding comparison, ACK and mailbox availability; received-reference/invocation TOKs; complete cycle append and Ready; all rejection/refusal routes. |
| Other original work | Every auxiliary source cycle and CaptureCAP, original counter/directory/fence/row/acquisition/ACK work; eventual original loan/client/terminal snapshot/verifier/receipt/consumer output/ACK and halt. |

For a successful general history flight its ordered bill is therefore

$$
\begin{aligned}
V_{\rm hist}={}&V_{\rm gate}+V_{\rm mode}+V_{\rm frame}
+V_{\rm Boundary}+V_{\rm cover/publication}+V_{\rm ClientCover}\\
&+V_{\rm bind}+V_{\rm Issue/publication}+V_{\rm ClientIssue}
+V_{\rm Call/Image/publication}+V_{\rm ClientImage/ACK}\\
&+V_{M/{\rm invocation}/Ready}.
\end{aligned}
$$

Each summand is evaluated at the previous one's full actual successor,
not at a separately optimized entry. Source CaptureCAP and the original
stopping flight are additional same-run contributors. A rejected flight
uses its actual shorter/changed rejection route in the same recurrence;
it is not billed for fictitious successful publications.

